"Holy",name=S[922],r=1,max=1},{tree="Holy",name="Holy Shock",r=1,max=1},{tree="Holy",name=S[989],r=2,max=2},{tree="Holy",name="Holy Power",r=5,max=5},{tree="Holy",name=S[923],r=1,max=1},{tree="Protection",name=S[505],r=5,max=5},{tree="Protection",name="Precision",r=3,max=3},{tree="Protection",name=S[978],r=2,max=2},{tree="Protection",name="Sacred Duty",r=1,max=2},{tree="Protection",name=S[616],r=1,max=1},{tree="Retribution",name="Benediction",r=5,max=5},{tree="Retribution",name="Conviction",r=3,max=3}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree="Holy",name=S[987],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=17,tree="Holy",name=S[1010],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=18,l2=19,tree="Holy",name="Reverence",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=20,l2=24,tree="Holy",name=S[1026],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=25,l2=25,tree="Holy",name=S[964],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=26,l2=27,tree="Holy",name=S[969],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=28,l2=28,tree="Holy",name=S[922],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=29,l2=29,tree="Holy",name=S[977],r1=1,r2=1,max=2},{l1=30,l2=30,tree="Holy",name="Holy Shock",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=31,l2=32,tree="Holy",name=S[989],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=33,l2=34,tree="Holy",name=S[988],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=35,l2=39,tree="Holy",name="Holy Power",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree="Holy",name=S[923],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Protection",name=S[505],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=46,l2=47,tree="Protection",name=S[978],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=48,l2=48,tree="Protection",name="Sacred Duty",r1=1,r2=1,max=2},{l1=49,l2=53,tree="Retribution",name="Benediction",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=54,l2=56,tree="Retribution",name="Conviction",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=57,l2=59,tree="Protection",name="Precision",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=60,l2=60,tree="Protection",name=S[616],r1=1,r2=1,max=1}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[684]},{t="h1",x="Holy",sub=S[778]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Heal single targets with Flash of Light and Holy Light, swear Oath of Light to your tank, and use Light’s Vigil with Holy Shock as your only party-wide heal."},{t="pills",list={S[702],"Dungeon healing",S[742]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[920]},{t="h2",x=S[589]},{t="p",x="These stages follow the talent order below. Holy is a group healing build: solo questing is slower than Retribution, so plan on dungeons and party play, and use Consecration, Judgement and Holy Strike for damage while questing."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Reliable casting"},{t="p",x="Keep a Seal up and use Holy Strike and Judgement while questing. Spiritual Focus 5/5 by 14 gives Flash of Light, Holy Light and Light’s Vigil a 70% chance to ignore pushback, then Healing Light 3/3 by 17 adds 12% healing and Reverence 2/2 by 19 lets 30% of your mana regeneration continue while casting."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Crits and Holy Shock"},{t="p",x="Flash of Light arrives at 20. Illumination 5/5 by 24 refunds half a heal’s base cost on every critical heal; Divine Favor (25), Infusion of Light (26–27) and Oath of Light (28) follow. Holy Shock arrives at 30 with Boundless Light 2/2 by 32, then Purifying Power and Holy Power 5/5 by 39 for 50% larger critical heals."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Vigil and support"},{t="p",x="Light’s Vigil at 40 gives you a party heal through Holy Shock. Divine Intellect 5/5 by 45 adds 10% Intellect, Guardian’s Favor (46–47) shortens Blessing of Protection, and Sacred Duty (48) shortens your immunities and Forbearance. Benediction 5/5 by 53 and Conviction 3/3 by 56 follow, then Precision (57–59) and Templar’s Bulwark (60) finish the build."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[630]},{t="h2",x=S[702]},{t="p",x=S[76]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[708]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[609]},{t="p",x=S[144]},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="Oath of Light replaces Blessing of Light in Forever: swear it to the ally you heal most, usually the tank. Boundless Light adds 30% Holy Shock critical chance on allies who are not under your Oath, and Illumination refunds mana on every critical heal, so Holy Power and critical chance pay for themselves."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[807]},{t="h2",x=S[662]},{t="p",x="Holy wants healing power first, then Intellect for your mana pool and spell crit. Illumination refunds mana on crits, so critical strike also helps your mana."},{t="h3",x=S[892]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[1011],x="or spell power"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Intellect",x="mana and spell crit"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Strength",x="for questing alone"},{t="p",s="small",x="When you quest alone, Strength and spell damage speed up kills; keep a healing set for dungeons."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[1011],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Intellect",x=""},{t="stat",i=3,b="Spirit",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Mana per 5",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Critical strike",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Healers do not need hit for heals. Some estimates rank critical strike above Spirit."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Mana per 5 keeps working while you cast; Spirit regeneration stops for 5 seconds after each spell that costs mana. The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[663]},{t="h2",x=S[726]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority list, not a fixed loop. Flash of Light arrives at 20, Holy Shock at 30 and Light’s Vigil at 40; before that, Holy Light is your heal."},{t="h4",x="Prepare the group"},{t="p",x="Give each player the right Blessing (Kings is the strongest default, Might for melee, Wisdom for casters) and keep an Aura up. Swear Oath of Light to the tank. Use Seal of Light while healing; it is your default healing Seal."},{t="h4",x="Flash of Light first"},{t="p",x="Flash of Light is your most efficient heal; use it to keep health topped up. Spiritual Focus protects it from pushback."},{t="h4",x="Holy Light for heavy damage"},{t="p",x="Switch to Holy Light when damage is high and you can afford it. Infusion of Light makes the next Holy Light 1 second faster after a critical Holy Shock or Flash of Light, and Divine Favor guarantees a critical heal when you need a big one."},{t="h4",x="Holy Shock and Light’s Vigil"},{t="p",x="Holy Shock is an instant heal for emergencies or while moving, but it is mana-hungry. Place Light’s Vigil on an ally before damage arrives; your next Holy Shock on them triggers no cooldown and heals their whole party. Boundless Light makes Holy Shock crit more often on allies outside your Oath."},{t="h4",x="Watch your mana"},{t="p",x="Mana is your limit. Let the five-second rule work between pulls, use Illumination refunds from critical heals, and ask for short breaks. While questing alone, use Seal of Righteousness, Judgement, Holy Strike and Consecration for damage."},{t="h4",x="Save the group"},{t="p",x="Cleanse (Purify before 42) removes poisons, diseases and magic. Blessing of Protection saves a caster from physical damage, Blessing of Freedom frees a rooted ally, and Lay on Hands is your emergency full heal. Divine Intervention (30) can save a healer from a wipe."},{t="abil",names={"Flash of Light","Holy Light","Holy Shock",S[923],S[922],S[964],"Seal of Light","Cleanse"}},{t="h3",x="Equipment and stats"},{t="p",x="Look for healing power, Intellect and mana regeneration first. Lighter armor with clearly better healing stats is fine, but keep enough Stamina to survive the damage that reaches you."},{t="p",x="Use a one-handed weapon with a shield or a held off-hand item. While questing alone, weapon damage, Strength and spell damage still help your Holy Strike, Seals and Consecration."},{t="h3",x="Supplies and group tips"},{t="p",x="Bring plenty of water and mana potions. Before each pull, check the tank has your Oath and the group has Blessings. Position where you can see the tank but not the pack."},{t="p",x="You have no interrupt; Hammer of Justice is your control. Redemption is learned through a level 12 class quest (The Tome of Divinity for Alliance, A Lesson in Divinity for Horde), so finish it before you start healing dungeons."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[779]},{t="h2",x=S[559]},{t="p",x=S[70]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[74]},{t="macro",n=S[727],x=S[299],code=S[379]},{t="macro",n=S[760],x=S[162],code=S[397]},{t="macro",n=S[631],x=S[108],code=S[225]},{t="macro",n=S[685],x=S[196],code=S[252]},{t="macro",n=S[761],x=S[262],code=S[286]},{t="macro",n=S[824],x=S[136],code=S[326]},{t="macro",n=S[610],x=S[312],code=S[226]},{t="macro",n=S[590],x=S[191],code=S[219]},{t="macro",n=S[591],x=S[240],code=S[414]},{t="macro",n="Holy Shock heal or damage",x="Heals the ally under your pointer or damages the enemy under it; otherwise uses your target, or yourself.",code="#showtooltip Holy Shock\n/cast [@mouseover,exists,nodead][exists,nodead][@player] Holy Shock"},{t="macro",n="Shift Light's Vigil, then Holy Shock",x="Hold Shift to place Light's Vigil on an ally, then press again without Shift after the global cooldown to Holy Shock the same ally. That Holy Shock heals their whole party and triggers no cooldown.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,@mouseover,help,nodead][mod:shift,help,nodead] Light's Vigil; [@mouseover,exists,nodead][exists,nodead][@player] Holy Shock"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Oath of Light",x="Swears Oath of Light to the ally under your pointer or your friendly target, usually your tank. Only one Oath can be active.",code="#showtooltip Oath of Light\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead] Oath of Light"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Lay on Hands",x="Emergency full heal on the ally under your pointer, your target or yourself. It uses all your remaining mana and has a long cooldown.",code="#showtooltip Lay on Hands\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead][@player] Lay on Hands"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[392]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[870]},{t="h2",x=S[611]},{t="p",x=S[83]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[84]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[44]},{t="widget",w="l